From 31c5aef703c6d5bba92288aa260f7229f13c68f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fi3 <you@example.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 01:23:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ADD strict selected-agent slash routing to prevent prompt
 fallback

Selected chat input beginning with a non-empty slash token executes through the backend command surface so unsupported provider commands fail explicitly instead of being delivered as ordinary prompts.
---
 docs/architecture.md  |  13 ++++-
 src/agent_runtime.rs  |  18 +++++++
 src/cli.rs            |  45 +++++++++++++++++
 src/codex.rs          | 114 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 tests/terminal_app.rs |  23 +++++++--
 tests/workspace.rs    |  71 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 224 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index b6ee24f..ad132c0 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -95,8 +95,13 @@ port when the requested address is unavailable.
 
 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::command` sends a backend-native command, such as `/status` or `/fork ...`, to an
+  existing agent session. The default implementation rejects the command explicitly so unsupported
+  providers do not receive backend commands as ordinary prompts.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
+- `AgentBackend::command_streaming` provides real-time output for backend-native commands. Its
+  default implementation calls `command`.
 - `AgentBackend::shutdown_handle` returns an `AgentShutdownHandle` for terminating active provider
   processes.
 - `AgentStreamEvent` carries status text, streamed agent messages, and streamed errors.
@@ -123,8 +128,9 @@ public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can parti
 - `SandboxMode` and `CodexCommandConfig` define Codex CLI invocation settings.
 - `CodexInvocation` records the command, arguments, and prompt used for an invocation.
 - `CodexBackend` stores Codex session history and implements `AgentBackend`.
-- `CodexBackend::build_launch_invocation` and `CodexBackend::build_send_invocation` construct
-  `codex exec` and `codex exec resume` calls. Launch invocations include the injected
+- `CodexBackend::build_launch_invocation`, `build_send_invocation`, and
+  `build_command_invocation` construct `codex exec` and `codex exec resume` calls. Launch
+  invocations include the injected
   `PromptPolicy`; resumed invocations for known sessions pass only the follow-up message because the
   Codex thread already contains the launch-time policy and repository instructions.
 - `CodexBackend::record_launch_reply`, `record_launch_output`, and `session` maintain in-memory
@@ -166,6 +172,9 @@ The primary public methods are:
 
 `CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.
 Workflow code must not hard-code `AgentKind::Codex` when the active profile supplies the provider.
+When selected-agent chat input begins with a slash followed by a non-whitespace token, `CommandChat`
+routes that input through `AgentBackend::command_streaming` instead of the ordinary prompt send path.
+Whitespace-only slash input, such as `/` or `/ status`, remains ordinary chat text.
 
 ## UI-Neutral Controller
 
